  "step1_summary": "• Chief complaint: 2-day history of constant dull ache in lower abdomen (below umbilicus) with associated nausea and feeling hot/sweaty.\n• Symptoms:\n  – Onset/duration: Gradual over the last 2-3 days.\n  – Character: Constant dull ache, makes her feel nauseated; no actual vomiting.\n  – Constitutional: Subjective fever (hot/sweaty); no light-headedness.\n  – GI/urinary: Previously constipated 1 week ago (now resolved, regular BM yesterday). Increased urinary frequency but no dysuria, urgency, foul smell or haematuria. No diarrhoea.\n  – Gynaecologic: Last menstrual period ~3 weeks ago; expects next period soon. Mild pink spotting over last couple of days. Sexually active with one partner. Uses etonogestrel implant (Implanon). No vaginal discharge. Unsure about pregnancy.\n• Past medical history: None reported.\n• Medications: Etonogestrel implant only.\n• Allergies: Amoxicillin allergy.\n• Family history: Brother with type 1 diabetes; otherwise non-contributory.\n• Social history: Non-smoker, lives with boyfriend.\n• Vital signs / exam: Tele-consult only – no vitals, no physical exam performed.\n• Labs / imaging: None to date.",
